('B', '**Identify (clinical).** Take a spiritual history: has the trauma strengthened or shaken faith? Listen for spiritual stuck points such as "God was punishing me," "God abandoned me," or "I can never be forgiven for what I did" (Currier et al., 2015; Fontana & Rosenheck, 2004).'),
('B', '**Challenge (clinical).** Examine the evidence for distorted self-blame (what could the person actually know or control at the time?). Separate true moral responsibility, which calls for confession and repair, from false guilt, which calls for correction (Litz et al., 2009; Resick et al., 2002).'),
('B', '**Replace (pastoral).** Offer Scripture of God’s presence, healing, and forgiveness:'),
